  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AI Weather for Action, Knowledge and Early response through Networks (AWAKEN)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will apply new advances in artificial intelligence to improve the timeliness, accuracy and usefulness of weather and impact information for people living in countries most affected by extreme weather. Work Package 1, which is funded separately within HMG, will focus on developing advanced AI based weather prediction methods that can complement existing forecasting systems. Work Package 2 will establish trusted and ethical standards for the use of AI in weather services, creating clear methods for evaluating the quality, fairness and reliability of new models. Work Package 3 will strengthen the ability to translate hazardous weather into expected real world impacts by improving how socio economic impacts are collected, assessed and connected to specific weather events. Work Package 4 will support national meteorological agencies to apply these new capabilities, helping them to integrate AI tools into their services, build long term skills and share knowledge across regions. Together, these activities aim to strengthen early warning systems, support earlier action ahead of severe weather, and help national institutions in low  and middle income countries use AI safely and sustainably. The overall goal is to reduce loss of life, protect livelihoods and ensure that the benefits of AI enabled forecasting are shared fairly with the communities that need them most.</narrative>
  </description>
